= Homework: Improper Integrals Practice

Evaluate the following improper integrals.
If the integral converges, compute its value.
If it diverges, explain why.

== Infinite Limits of Integration

#enum(
$
integral_1^infinity 1/x^2 dif x
$,

$
integral_1^infinity 1/x dif x
$,

$
integral_2^infinity 1/x^3 dif x
$,

$
integral_0^infinity e^(-x) dif x
$
)

== Infinite Discontinuities at an Endpoint

#enum(
$
integral_0^1 1/sqrt(x) dif x
$,

$
integral_0^1 1/x^(2/3) dif x
$,

$
integral_0^1 ln(x) dif x
$,

$
integral_0^1 1/x dif x
$
)

== Discontinuities Inside the Interval

Determine whether the following integrals converge. Split the integral if necessary.

#enum(
$
integral_-1^1 1/x^2 dif x
$,

$
integral_-1^1 1/x dif x
$
)

== Mixed and More Challenging

#enum(
$
integral_1^infinity (1/x^2 + 1/x^3) dif x
$,

$
integral_0^infinity x e^(-x) dif x
$
)